- **Boundary:** Markup attributes
  - **What to validate:** `select` (single-choice) — its choice, keys and typeahead, click, the `selected` attribute, an option's `label` · `value`, the `change` event
  - **How (stack-specific):** In every document, remote pages included: a `select` without `multiple` holds its choice as its options' `CHECKED` state, seeded from a `selected` attribute at creation, a `selected` write exclusive and a cleared one unchosen, every recorded select settled at the mutator's flush and on entering the document by HTML's selectedness setting algorithm — the last chosen, else the first option not disabled; a `multiple` write or removal records the select, so removal settles it to one, and `set_option_selectedness` leaves a `multiple` select's other options alone (packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1262-1271; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/element.rs:472-478; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1041-1044; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1134-1138; packages/blitz-dom/src/mutator.rs:1273-1295; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select.rs:258-267); its rules, cited to the WHATWG `select` element, read the select's `option` children and those of its `optgroup` children, in tree order (the `optgroup` row), an option's label (its non-empty `label` attribute, else its stripped and collapsed text) and its value (its `value` attribute, else the text) (packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select.rs:18-304); on a focused single-choice select that `ElementData::is_disabled` does not read disabled, a pressed `ArrowDown` / `ArrowUp` takes the next / previous enabled option, `Home` / `End` the first / last, a `Key::Character` with no Ctrl, Alt or Meta is typeahead and every other key does nothing (Enter and Space open nothing) — a closed key match (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:108-113; packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:171-255); typeahead keeps the typed text in the document's private `select_typeahead` buffer, starting afresh for another select or after 1 s of the document's clock, and chooses the first enabled option whose label starts with it, compared in lower case, an empty text matching nothing — compared, never kept past 1 s and never carried out (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:303-324; packages/blitz-dom/src/node/select.rs:294-304);
 a click on a select, past `handle_click`'s `is_disabled` walk gate, clears the typeahead and the text selection and focuses it (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/pointer.rs:875-888); every choice goes through one path that marks the changed set and dispatches `input` then the engine-emitted `change` (not cancelable, bubbling), each carrying `BaseDocument::select_value`, a choice of the chosen option firing nothing (packages/blitz-dom/src/events/keyboard.rs:382-408; packages/blitz-traits/src/events.rs:150; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/dioxus_document.rs:393-398); the choice leaves only as form submission's entries (every chosen option not disabled, packages/blitz-dom/src/form.rs:276-286), the `input` and `change` events' value, the snapshot's `value` (the chosen option's value, no mask applying) and the options' tree nodes — an option under a select kept in the accessibility tree though it computes `display: none`, its `selected` written from its state, its `label` attribute its name (packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:164-170; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:184-194; packages/blitz-dom/src/accessibility.rs:280-281; packages/dioxus-native-dom/src/snapshot.rs:242-261) — inside the ratified name and control-value crossings; the driver's `type` on a single select is the same typeahead (a `multiple` select's, its own row below), its help one fixed sentence more (packages/escher-driver/src/schema.rs:238-240); no print, log site, env read or panic path in the rules module, and no carrier, verb, argument, key name, result field, cause, session error, exit, log field or span added; stated limits: no popup is painted, Enter and Space open nothing on a single select, an option of a closed single select has no click arm and stays refused `covered`, under a group too, and `size` is not read; pinned by the rules module's 8 unit tests, `select_interaction` 18 and `stand_act_select` 10, both layout modes, as measured at escher-0.3.0/chunks/2026-10-31-engine-debts/report.md (tests/blitz-tests/tests/select_interaction.rs:123-353;
 tests/blitz-tests/tests/stand_act_select.rs:84-261) — an engine change for every document and a boundary widening, ratified — as measured at escher-0.2.0/chunks/2026-10-20-select-by-id/report.md
